## Technical Requirements

- It is necessary to always use ready-made libraries if they exist on the internet.
- For all strings displayed to the user, internationalization should be used.
- Do not edit Info.plist and entitlements directly. All changes must be made only through Project.swift, processed by Tuist.
- Do not include files from Common. They are included by Project.swift as a source.
- Use logging instead of prints to receive more
- ALWAYS USE DEVOPS-FRIENDLY FLOW:
    - NO MANUAL WORK IN XCODE GUI.
    - ALL CONFIGURATION THROUGH FILES (`Project.swift`, `.xcconfig`, `plist`, ETC.).
    - REPRODUCIBLE BUILDS VIA `tuist generate`, `xcodebuild`.
    - SIGNING, PROVISIONING, AND VERSIONING AUTOMATED.
    - ALL TOOLS CLI-BASED, INTEGRATED WITH CI/CD.
